                  "explanation": "A forbidden plane is a range of motion that your body is biologically capable of but that some rule — usually a clinical edge case generalized too far — taught you to avoid. The tissue never gets exposed, never builds capacity, and then fails when real life inevitably uses it (like Sarah's toddler lift). Option D inverts the truth: forbidden planes are dangerous because they're avoided, not avoided because they're dangerous."
