                  "explanation": "Sarah's deadlift was strong because she trained that exact shape for six years. But six years of training one shape — neutral spine, braced core, sagittal hinge — built zero capacity in the rounded, rotated, off-axis shape real life eventually demanded. The 245 pounds proved nothing about her tolerance at 22 pounds in a different geometry. Capacity in one plane doesn't generalize to capacity in every plane; it has to be specifically built. The rules that kept her gym-safe made her toddler-fragile."
