                  "explanation": "Tom had plenty of passive length — that's not what failed him. What failed was his active control and brain map at the end range of his hip. CARs combine active muscle work, joint sensory feedback, and conscious attention at the edge of range. That trio expands the joint's cortical map in 2-4 weeks. Passive stretching feels good but cannot grow the wiring that defends the joint when a sudden load arrives. Daily CARs are the difference between range you have and range you can actually use."
