                  "explanation": "Consolidation is the 6-24 hour neurological process after a practice session where the motor cortex strengthens the synapses involved in that pattern. This happens once per session, regardless of session length. That's why seven 10-minute daily sessions produce more skill consolidation than one 70-minute weekly session — same total time, but seven consolidation cycles instead of one."
