                  "explanation": "The transverse plane — rotation and twisting — is the most neglected in standard gym programs that focus on squats, deadlifts, presses, and pulls. Yet real life is full of rotation: reaching for seatbelts, twisting to pick up children, turning to grab bags. Because untrained rotational patterns combine with unexpected loads in unpredictable positions, this is exactly where most adult tweaks and back injuries happen."
