                  "explanation": "Tendons are load-adapted tissue. Complete passive rest leads to tendon atrophy and weaker collagen — when activity resumes, re-injury is more likely. The modern evidence base (Alfredson, Kongsgaard, Cook) shows tendons need specific mechanical stress to remodel: heavy slow resistance, isometrics, and controlled eccentrics. After 40 this is even more important because remodeling time doubles. A is the outdated \"rest it\" myth. C and D address muscle and fascia, not the tendon's actual rebuilding need."
