                  "title": "Final Synthesis Check",
                  "content": "Pulling together everything in MovesMethod, which statement **best** captures the philosophy?\n\nA. Mobility is a program you complete in 6-12 weeks to fix tight muscles\nB. Mobility is a daily, lifelong practice of training varied movement patterns and visiting end-ranges so the body remains open, resilient, and adapted to whatever ordinary life demands\nC. Mobility is just stretching before workouts to prevent injury\nD. Mobility is mostly genetic — you either have it or you don't\n\n---\n\n**Answer: B**\n\n**Explanation:** The entire MovesMethod arc — joint capsules need use, tissues adapt to load, breath drives the system, variety builds resilience, age changes the dose, snacks beat sessions — all points to the same conclusion: **mobility is not a program**. It is a **lifestyle of consistent, varied, end-range movement woven into ordinary life**, scaled honestly to the body you actually have, tracked in decades. A is the \"fix it\" myth. C reduces a way of being to a pre-workout chore. D contradicts every page of the evidence — mobility is highly trainable at every age. The body remains open because the life remains open.",
